[metal] Present inside the Core Animation transaction when the layer asks for it

The Metal swapchain presents its drawable from the command buffer
([MTLCommandBuffer presentDrawable:]), which reaches the screen on its own
schedule, a frame or more away from the Core Animation layer changes made in
the same main-thread step. A CAMetalLayer with presentsWithTransaction set asks
for the opposite: the drawable is presented with [CAMetalDrawable present]
after the work is scheduled, so it lands in the current transaction.
SkiaView sets that flag, so a canvas moved by an animated value presents in
the same transaction as the views moved alongside it.

The same change is commit 9c560c615 on github.com/Jaltaire/dawn
(branch main-jaltaire), on the Dawn commit Skia pins. Drop this patch once
the pinned Dawn honours presentsWithTransaction itself: build-dawn.ts skips it
when it is already present and fails when it no longer applies.

diff --git a/src/dawn/native/metal/SwapChainMTL.mm b/src/dawn/native/metal/SwapChainMTL.mm
index b9a9d07b3..0a9794f2c 100644
--- a/src/dawn/native/metal/SwapChainMTL.mm
+++ b/src/dawn/native/metal/SwapChainMTL.mm
@@ -95,9 +95,14 @@ MaybeError SwapChain::PresentImpl() {
     DAWN_ASSERT(mCurrentDrawable != nullptr);
 
     Queue* queue = ToBackend(GetDevice()->GetQueue());
-    CommandRecordingContext* commandContext = queue->GetPendingCommandContext();
-    [commandContext->GetCommands() presentDrawable:*mCurrentDrawable];
-    DAWN_TRY(queue->SubmitPendingCommandBuffer());
+    if ([*mLayer presentsWithTransaction]) {
+        queue->WaitForCommandsToBeScheduled();
+        [*mCurrentDrawable present];
+    } else {
+        CommandRecordingContext* commandContext = queue->GetPendingCommandContext();
+        [commandContext->GetCommands() presentDrawable:*mCurrentDrawable];
+        DAWN_TRY(queue->SubmitPendingCommandBuffer());
+    }
 
     mTexture->APIDestroy();
     mTexture = nullptr;
